$ ===================== UNIFIED LOADS + COMBINATIONS (audit thread, unchanged) =====================
!#!Info 26016 HPC Kier BAM JV - unified parametric loads + combinations (SOFiLOAD + ASE + MAXIMA)
!
! Version 3, 2026-10-19. v3: L2 stair voids (#STV), no deck load over the stair cut-outs. v2 2026-10-16. Generated from your export '26016 HPC Kier BAM JV_exp.dat' (2026-10-16).
! Run in Teddy INSIDE the 26016 project (same database). This one file replaces:
!   - load cases 2-4, 11-16, 21-28, 31-68, 71-74, 91-92 (SSD load tasks and 26016_stairs_loads.dat) and
!   - the COPY-built combinations 101-118 / 201-213 and the MAXIMA envelopes of 26016_stairs_loads.dat.
! After the first run, do not re-run the old load definitions. Load case numbers keep their old meaning
! (21-24 = deck wind incl. uplift, 25-28 stairs wind, 71-74 = 21-24 + 25-28), so an old task run by
! mistake brings back old VALUES but cannot double a load.
!
! NO DUPLICATION BY CONSTRUCTION
!   - Every load value is written once, as an expression of the parameters below.
!   - Groups are defined once (#GL permanent, #QL / #QI imposed, #HL roof); combinations loop over them,
!     so each basic load case enters a combination exactly once. Self-weight comes only from FACD.
!   - Wind enters every combination as ONE direction with one factor:
!       uplift combinations   = 21-24 (lateral + canopy uplift) + 25-28 (stairs)
!       downward combinations = 81-84 (lateral) + 25-28 (stairs) + 85-88 (roof downward)
!     81-88 and 25-28 are building blocks with TYPE '-' (no action), so no automatic superposition can
!     add them a second time. 71-78 hold the same complete cases for MAXIMA.
!   - MAXIMA lists every load case explicitly (no 'LC NO -1'), so other load cases in the database
!     (eigen mass cases, old patterns) are never picked up. Full-deck LL (11, 13, action QF) is used in the
!     named combinations only; the MAXIMA envelope uses the patterns instead. Never superpose QF with QB.
!   - MAXIMA results are stored from 4101 up, clear of the eigen modes 2001-2010 / 2101-2110.
!
! DESIGN TOOLS: read ULS 101-130 and 135-154 (or the MAXIMA envelope 4301+). 101-118 alone are all wind-with-
! uplift cases and miss wind with roof downward (119-130), barriers inward (135), temperature (136-139), the
! sway imperfection with gravity only (141-148) and the per-span LL patterns (151-154, combination 102 with the
! deck LL rearranged, for BDK / AQB). EQU 131-134 are for overall equilibrium (holding down) only.
! EHF: in every ULS wind combination (wind direction) and in 141-148. 135-139 carry none: inward barriers and
! uniform temperature are self-equilibrating on the ring; the MAXIMA ULS envelope (4101+) combines them with EHF.
!
! SETTINGS: every value is a parameter (STO#...) in the SOFiLOAD block. Values marked CONFIRM need your input.
! Values marked NEW change the results compared with your current model. With every parameter set to its
! [legacy] value, all basic load cases and combinations 101-118, 201 and 206-209 reproduce your export
! (checked record by record). 202-205 are deliberately new (G + W + psi0 Q, EN 1990 eq 6.14b) and 210-213
! use the single wind psi0 (your export used 0.6 for ULS but 0.5 for SLS).
! Z is up: +PG = down, PZP/PZZ negative = down, PG negative = uplift.
!
+PROG SOFILOAD urs:5
HEAD 26016 unified loads + combinations
UNIT TYPE 5

$ ---------- code basis (EN 1990 + UK National Annex assumed) ----------
STO#GSUP   1.35       $ gamma G unfavourable, EN 1990 Table A1.2(B), eq 6.10
STO#GINF   1          $ gamma G favourable, Table A1.2(B)
STO#GEQU   0.9        $ gamma G,inf for EQU (overall uplift/overturning), Table A1.2(A) + UK NA
STO#GQ     1.5        $ gamma Q
STO#PSIQ   0.7        $ psi0 imposed Cat C (deck, stairs, barriers)
STO#PSIQ1  0.7        $ psi1 Cat C
STO#PSIQ2  0.6        $ psi2 Cat C
STO#PSIW   0.5        $ psi0 wind, UK NA Table NA.A1.1 (EN recommended 0.6)   [legacy 0.6]
STO#PSIH   0.7        $ psi0 roof imposed Cat H, UK NA Table NA.A1.1 (EN recommended 0)
STO#PSIT   0.6        $ psi0 temperature
STO#HLEAD  1          $ 1 = roof imposed load taken at full gamma Q with the deck LL when LL leads (as before, conservative)
STO#HWIND  0          $ 1 = roof imposed load also in the wind combinations. EN 1991-1-1 3.3.2(1): not together (0)   [legacy 1]

$ ---------- combination factors, derived from the values above (do not edit; COPY FACT takes a plain #name only) ----------
STO#GQW    #GQ*#PSIW  $ gamma Q x psi0 wind
STO#GQQ    #GQ*#PSIQ  $ gamma Q x psi0 imposed
STO#GQH    #GQ*#PSIH  $ gamma Q x psi0 roof
STO#GQT    #GQ*#PSIT  $ gamma Q x psi0 temperature
STO#FH     #GQ*IIF(#HLEAD,1,#PSIH) $ factor on roof imposed load when the deck LL leads
STO#FHW    #FH*#HWIND $ the same in wind combinations
STO#GQHW   #GQH*#HWIND $ gamma Q x psi0 roof in wind combinations
STO#PSIHW  #PSIH*#HWIND $ psi0 roof in SLS wind combinations

$ ---------- permanent loads ----------
STO#SDLF   0.89       $ kPa floor finishes + panels, L1 + L2 (consultant 7.7(a))
STO#SDLR   0.046      $ kPa roof
STO#HR     0.4        $ kN/m handrail, deck perimeters and stairs
STO#WALL   1          $ kN/m core walls at r = 3 m, L1 + L2
STO#DLF    0.2        $ kPa extra dead load on all floors (Wing 2026-10-15)
STO#STV    1          $ 1 = L2 stair voids open (r 8.5-12 at 260-300 and 20-60 deg (v17; was 40-80), Wing 2026-10-19): no deck load there (NEW v3), 0 = full sectors   [legacy 0]
STO#NSTV   1-#STV     $ derived (do not edit): 1 when the stair voids are loaded as deck
STO#SDLL   0          $ kPa landing deck SDL (LAR 601-604), 0 = none as before. CONFIRM
STO#BST    2.08       $ m stair width between stringers

$ ---------- imposed loads ----------
STO#LL     5          $ kPa decks, UK NA Table NA.3 C5
STO#LLR    0.6        $ kPa roof, UK NA Table NA.7 Cat H (roof not publicly accessible). CONFIRM
STO#LLS    5          $ kPa stairs + landings
STO#BAR    3          $ kN/m stair barrier, UK NA Table NA.8 C5
STO#HBR    1.1        $ m stair barrier height above stringer
STO#BARD   0          $ v4: deck barriers LC 17/18 OFF (Wing 18 Oct)   was 3,  kN/m deck perimeter barrier L1 + L2, UK NA Table NA.8 C5 (NEW; 0 = off)   [legacy 0]
STO#HBRD   1.1        $ m deck barrier height above the edge beam
STO#PATR   1          $ LL patterns: 1 = per sector AND per radial span (NEW, LC 301-358/401-458), 0 = whole sectors (LC 31-68)   [legacy 0]

$ ---------- wind (EN 1991-1-4) - qp = ce x 0.613 x vb^2 ----------
STO#VB     25         $ m/s basic wind velocity. CONFIRM (UK NA vb,map x calt x cdir x cseason x cprob)
STO#CE     2          $ exposure factor ce(z). CONFIRM: coastal site, z = 12 m gives about 2.7-3.1
STO#Q      0.5        $ kPa peak velocity pressure qp. v20 (Wing 13 Nov 2026): 0.500 kPa for all wind loads (v19m: #CE*0.613*#VB**2/1000 = 0.766)
STO#BCL    3          $ m cladding width per enclosure column (ground r 8.5, core r 3)
STO#DR     0.15       $ m width of raking columns / struts (RHS 150)
STO#CFR    1.45       $ cf RHS 150x150 (EN 7.6: 2.1 x psi_r 0.75 x psi_lambda 0.92). CONFIRM   [legacy 1]
STO#EDGE   1          $ 1 = wind on deck edge beams + open balustrade (NEW), 0 = off   [legacy 0]
STO#CFE    2          $ cf deck edge beam (I-section, EN 7.7)
STO#DE1    0.254      $ m L1 edge beam depth (UB 254)
STO#DE2    0.457      $ m L2 edge beam depth (UB 457)
STO#DE3    0.254      $ m roof edge beam depth (UB 254)
STO#CFL    1.8        $ cf open balustrade (plane lattice, EN 7.11)
STO#PHIB   0.3        $ balustrade solidity ratio (glass or solid infill: 1.0 with CFL about 1.2). CONFIRM
STO#HBAL   1.1        $ m balustrade height
STO#LEE    0          $ factor on the LEEWARD edge beam: 0 = in the wake of the deck (deck drag counted once, cf EN 8.3)
STO#LEEB   1          $ factor on the LEEWARD balustrade (1.0 = no shielding, 24 m apart)
STO#CPU    1          $ uplift cf on the roof (x qp). CONFIRM: EN Table 7.6 alpha 0 gives 0.5 (empty below) to 1.3 (blocked)
STO#CPUD   1          $ uplift coefficient on L1 + L2 decks (your deck rule)
STO#CPD    0.2        $ downward cf on the roof, EN Table 7.6 alpha 0 overall max (NEW wind cases 75-78)
STO#ECC    1          $ ROOF: 1 = resultant at d/4 from windward edge, EN 1991-1-4 Fig 7.16 (NEW, peak 2.8 x average), 0 = uniform   [legacy 0]
STO#ECCD   0          $ L1 + L2 decks: 0 = uniform uplift (your deck rule), 1 = resultant at d/4 as the roof
STO#D5     0.20       $ m stair RHS 200x100 depth facing the wind (v16; model section 5, was 0.25 for RHS 250x150)
STO#D6     0.05       $ m stair RHS 50x50
STO#D9     0.08       $ m SHS 80x80 (v19 external stair legs + transverse beams)
STO#D8     0.10       $ m SHS 100x100 depth facing the wind (v17 external stair legs + ring brackets, section 8)
STO#CF5    1.5        $ cf stair RHS sect 5
STO#CF6    1.2        $ cf stair RHS 50x50
STO#VF     1          $ 1 = wind pressure on inclined stair flights (Table 7.6 canopy method)
STO#UPL    0          $ 1 = uplift -qp on stair landings

$ ---------- temperature (EN 1991-1-5) ----------
STO#DTP    15         $ K uniform expansion. CONFIRM (exposed steel, UK, T0 10 C)
STO#DTN    -15        $ K uniform contraction. CONFIRM
STO#TSH    1          $ 1 = temperature also on kingpost shells + plates (NEW), 0 = beams only   [legacy 0]

$ ---------- sway imperfection (EN 1993-1-1 5.3.2) as equivalent horizontal forces ----------
STO#EHF    1          $ 1 = add EHF to the ULS wind combinations (wind direction) and to 141-148 (NEW). 0 if ASE imperfections are used   [legacy 0]
STO#HTOT   12.2       $ m height for alpha_h
STO#MCOL   1          $ m columns for alpha_m (1 = conservative)
STO#PHI    1/200*MAX(2/3,MIN(1,2/SQR(#HTOT)))*SQR(0.5*(1+1/#MCOL)) $ sway imperfection phi
STO#RHOS   78.5       $ kN/m3 steel (EHF from member self-weight)

$ ---------- actions (factors come from the parameters above) ----------
ACT 'G'   GAMU #GSUP #GINF PSI0 1 1 1 1 PART 'G' SUP PERM TITL "Permanent SW+SDL"
ACT 'QF'  GAMU #GQ 0 PSI0 #PSIQ #PSIQ1 #PSIQ2 #PSIQ1 PART 'Q' SUP COND TITL "LL full decks (named combos)"
ACT 'QB'  GAMU #GQ 0 PSI0 #PSIQ #PSIQ1 #PSIQ2 #PSIQ1 PART 'Q' SUP COND TITL "LL patterns+stairs+barriers"
ACT 'QH'  GAMU #GQ 0 PSI0 #PSIH 0 0 0 PART 'Q' SUP COND TITL "Roof imposed Cat H"
ACT 'W'   GAMU #GQ 0 PSI0 #PSIW 0.2 0 1 PART 'Q' SUP EXCL TITL "Wind complete cases"
ACT 'T'   GAMU #GQ 0 PSI0 #PSIT 0.5 0 1 PART 'Q' SUP EXCL TITL "Temperature"
ACT 'EHF' GAMU 1 0 PSI0 1 1 1 1 PART 'Q' SUP EXCL TITL "Sway imperfection EHF"

