$ ===================== BDK BUCKLING CHECK OF ALL MEMBERS (LTB thread, unchanged) =====================
!#!Info 26016 HPC Kier BAM JV - buckling check of ALL members (BDK, EN 1993-1-1 6.3 with the UK NA values)
!
! Version 1, 2026-10-16. Generated by generator/gen_buckling_all.py from your export '26016 HPC Kier BAM JV_exp.dat'
! (16 Oct 2026). Supersedes 26016_ltb_bdk.dat v2: the UB part is repeated here unchanged (same switches, same
! restraint logic), and the SHS columns, the rakers and the stair members are added.
! UNTESTED in SOFiSTiK: if the CADINP echo shows an error, send the line.
!
! WHAT EACH MEMBER TYPE GETS (one MEMB record per member, TYPE LTB = bending + axial force, 6.3.1 + 6.3.2 + 6.3.3)
!   UB 254x146x43 / UB 457x191x89 (groups 15, 25, 35, open I-sections): lateral torsional buckling 6.3.2.3 (chi_LT, Mcr
!     by eigenvalue analysis with the restraints below), flexural buckling 6.3.1 about y and z, interaction 6.61 / 6.62
!     with the Annex B Table B.2 factors (members susceptible to torsional deformation), Method 2.
!   SHS 150x150x10 columns and rakers (section 1, groups 11, 12, 13, 14, 21, 23, 24, 31, 34) and the RHS stair members (sections 5
!     and 6, group 60): flexural buckling 6.3.1 about y and z (Ncr by eigenvalue analysis of the pinned member, Lcr = L)
!     and interaction 6.61 / 6.62, Method 2. Lateral torsional buckling is evaluated too, on the UK NA route (Table NA.1
!     row 'rolled I and H sections and hot-finished hollow sections', h/b <= 2 -> curve b, lambda_LT,0 0.4, beta 0.75):
!     hand estimate with Mcr = (pi/L) sqrt(E Iz G It): lambda_LT = 0.23 for a 5.8 m raker, 0.19 for a 4 m column, 0.20 for
!     a 4 m stair flight, all below the plateau 0.4, so chi_LT = 1.0 and the hollow sections are governed by flexural
!     buckling and the interaction, as expected (SHS: not susceptible to LTB, 6.3.2.1(2), RHS 250x150: 6.3.2.2(4)).
!     Interaction factors: CTRL LTB AUTO lets BDK pick Table B.1 (not susceptible to torsional deformation) or B.2 by
!     section type, the manual does not enumerate the literals, so check in the ECHO MEMB FULL output of one raker that
!     kzy = 0.6 kyy (Table B.1). If BDK used B.2 the result is still a valid, slightly different interaction.
!   Stair connection stubs shorter than 0.3 m: not checked (listed under MODEL FACTS), the section check is AQB's job.
!   Stair treads (300 x 5 mm plates modelled as beams, section 7): no member buckling, not checked. Kingpost and ground
!     slab shells (SAR): not members, not checked (shell buckling of the kingpost would need an ASE buckling run).
!   CHS 610x20 (section 3) is defined in AQUA but no structural line uses it.
!
! CODE VALUES (EN 1993-1-1 with the UK National Annex, BS NA to BS EN 1993-1-1:2005)
!   - Flexural buckling curves, Table 6.2: UB h/b > 1.2, tf <= 40 mm -> a (y-y), b (z-z). Hollow sections: your AQUA
!     sets them explicitly, SECT 1/5/6 ... BCY 'A' BCZ 'A' = curve a = hot finished (EN 10210, PROF TYPE 'RHS').
!     If the SHS/RHS are COLD FORMED (EN 10219) the curve is c: change BCY/BCZ to 'C' (and, for consistency, PROF TYPE
!     'RHS' to 'RHSC') in the model's AQUA input and re-run the model, and set #COLD 1 below (LTB curve c, Table NA.1
!     row 'welded sections and cold-formed hollow sections'). BDK has no switch for the flexural curve itself.
!     This is the open hot/cold question from the report thread.
!   - LTB of the UBs: 6.3.2.3 rolled sections, lambda_LT,0 = 0.4, beta = 0.75 (UK NA NA.2.17 = EN), curve from Table NA.1
!     by h/b: UB 254x146x43 (1.76) -> b, UB 457x191x89 (2.41) -> c, set with CTRL CURV. kc = 1/sqrt(C1) from BDK's
!     eigenvalue analysis (CTRL TAB NO, BDK default, DIN NA relation C1 = kc^-2), UK NA NA.2.18 names Table 6.6, so set
!     CTRL TAB YES if you read it as Table 6.6 only (both give kc 0.94 for a UDL on a simple span).
!   - Interaction: Method 2 (Annex B) for every member (CTRL MTHD 2), gamma_M1 = 1.00 (TVAR GAM-S1, UK NA NA.2.15 = EN).
!   - Cross-section class from AQB automatically (SCL AUTO), S275 from the project materials.
!   - The project NORM stays 'EN' '199x-200x' COUN 0: for these sections the UK NA and the EN defaults coincide.
!
! COLUMNS AND RAKERS - READ THIS
!   Every column and raker is checked alone between its end nodes with fork supports (pinned, Lcr = L about both axes).
!   That is right for a NON-SWAY frame, EN 1993-1-1 5.2.1(3): alpha_cr >= 10 for every ULS combination. Nothing in the
!   model proves that yet: run 26016_buckling_alphacr_ase.dat (ASE buckling eigenvalues for the governing combinations)
!   and read the first positive buckling factor of each. If alpha_cr >= 10 everywhere, this file is complete.
!   If alpha_cr < 10: re-solve the sway combinations 145-148 (and the wind cases you need) with SYST PROB TH2 (the
!   -PROG block in that file), so the member forces include the P-delta effects on the imperfect frame, then run this
!   file with #SWAY 1 (Cmy = Cmz = 0.9 for the columns, Table B.3) - the member lengths then stay Lcr = L, 5.2.2(7)b.
!   The V-column rakers meet at an apex on the r 12 ring beam: each raker is one line, checked alone.
!   In a sway frame only combinations that carry the imperfection EHF and are solved with TH2 are covered by 5.2.2(7)b:
!   103-130 and 141-148 carry EHF, 101-102, 135-139 and 151-154 do not (for the columns, 145-148 are those with EHF).
!
! RESTRAINTS OF THE UB BEAMS (unchanged from 26016_ltb_bdk.dat v2, every value is a parameter below)
!   - Member ends: fork supports (CY CZ DX fixed, bending and warping free) = BDK default, written explicitly.
!     #AUTO 1 instead takes the end springs from a linear analysis of the whole model (BDK literal AUTO).
!   - Along a radial beam, every ring beam crossing is a lateral restraint at the ring-beam end plate (CY FIX,
!     height #EZR from the beam axis, 0 = shear centre). Twist restraint there:
!       column meets the beam at that point (end plates clamp both flanges) -> DX FIX,
!       ring beams only (pinned in the model, FIXA/FIXE 'MY')         -> DX #DXR, default 0 = no twist restraint.
!   - The deck panels give NO restraint by default (#DECK 0). If the panels are fixed to the top flange and act as
!     a diaphragm, set #DECK 1: lateral restraint at the top flange every L/#NPART (CVL HDIV ... EZ TOP).
!   - L1 and roof radial beams are three structural lines (r 12-8.5, 8.5-3, 3-inner), #JOIN 1 checks each radial
!     as ONE continuous member (MEMB + CONT) with the restraints above, so the moment diagram over the supports is
!     kept. #JOIN 0 checks each structural line on its own with fork ends (assumes twist restraint at every ring).
!     Run both and compare: the larger utilisation governs unless you can justify twist restraint at every ring.
!   - Intermediate VERTICAL supports inside a joined member are not modelled by BDK (no such item): the LTB mode is
!     unaffected (My and the loads come from ASE), but Ncr,y is computed on the full joined length, so n-y and kyy
!     come out conservative. N is small in these beams. If n-y matters, add SKY = longest span / L to that MEMB
!     record (value in the member's comment line): BDK then uses the Euler length SKY x L for Ncr,y only, Mcr stays
!     from the eigenvalue analysis (BDK manual, flexural buckling flow chart and the Schneider 8-41 example).
!   - Ring beams: chords between radials, fork ends. r 12 and r 8.5 rings are checked, the r 3 and r 1.9 rings
!     (1.04 m / 0.66 m) only with #RING3 1.
!   - Stair stringers, posts and landing members: each line alone, fork ends, the treads are not counted as restraints.
!
! LOAD HEIGHT (UB beams) - the deck loads are AREA loads, passed to the beams at the beam axis, so BDK sees them at the
!   shear centre. A top-flange load on an unrestrained beam is destabilising (Mcr about 20-30 % lower). BDK has no
!   load-height item. Run 26016_ltb_benchmark.dat FIRST: it shows whether BDK lowers Mcr for a load given with an
!   eccentricity. Until that is proven, treat the sagging checks of beams with #DECK 0 as needing a hand check with
!   zg = h/2 (hand values in the benchmark header), or set #DECK 1 if the deck really restrains the top flange.
!
! RESULTS
!   ECHO SUM FULL prints one line per member: the maximum utilisation over all combinations and its load case.
!   The envelope is stored in LC 9100 (CTRL LCST) for WinGRAF / Result Viewer (beam utilisation).
!   The second program (-PROG, switched off) prints the full tables (Mcr, C1, lambda_LT, chi_LT, Mb,Rd, chi_y, chi_z,
!   k-factors) for the members you list there: switch it on with +PROG once you know the governing members.
!
! RUN ORDER: 26016_loads_unified.dat (SOFiLOAD + ASE + MAXIMA, including LC 151-154) in the 26016 project, then this
!   file (and 26016_buckling_alphacr_ase.dat for the columns, see above). BDK needs the ASE results of LC 101-154
!   computed from real loads (they are: the combinations are COPY-built load cases). If your copy of the unified
!   file lacks 151-154, set #PAT 0.
!   Run time: 311 members with the default switches (166 UB + 145 hollow-section members, 379 member
!   blocks in the file) x 43 or 47 combinations, each with its own eigenvalue analysis: expect minutes, not seconds.
!   Use the switches to run one group at a time.
!
! MODEL FACTS USED (from the export):
!   L1: 18 radial beams, ring radii [1.9, 3.0, 8.5, 12.0]
!      12 x 3 SLN, L 10.1 m, stations (r, column?) ((3.0, False), (8.5, True))
!      6 x 3 SLN, L 10.1 m, stations (r, column?) ((3.0, True), (8.5, True))
!      1 radials whose structural lines run in opposite directions (checked line by line, not joined): 320 deg
!      ring r 1.9: 18 chords, L 0.66 m, pinned ends: True, columns at ends: 0
!      ring r 3.0: 18 chords, L 1.04 m, pinned ends: False, columns at ends: 12
!      ring r 8.5: 18 chords, L 2.95 m, pinned ends: True, columns at ends: 18
!      ring r 12.0: 18 chords, L 4.17 m, pinned ends: False, columns at ends: 18
!   L2: 18 radial beams, ring radii [3.0, 8.5, 12.0]
!      2 x 1 SLN, L 7.84 m, stations (r, column?) ((3.0, False),)
!      10 x 1 SLN, L 11.34 m, stations (r, column?) ((3.0, False), (8.5, False))
!      4 x 1 SLN, L 11.34 m, stations (r, column?) ((3.0, True), (8.5, False))
!      2 x 1 SLN, L 11.34 m, stations (r, column?) ((3.0, True), (8.5, True))
!      ring r 3.0: 18 chords, L 1.04 m, pinned ends: True, columns at ends: 12
!      ring r 8.5: 18 chords, L 2.95 m, pinned ends: True, columns at ends: 6
!      ring r 12.0: 18 chords, L 4.17 m, pinned ends: False, columns at ends: 18
!   roof: 18 radial beams, ring radii [3.0, 8.5, 12.0]
!      12 x 3 SLN, L 11.34 m, stations (r, column?) ((3.0, False), (8.5, False))
!      6 x 3 SLN, L 11.34 m, stations (r, column?) ((3.0, True), (8.5, False))
!      1 radials whose structural lines run in opposite directions (checked line by line, not joined): 320 deg
!      ring r 3.0: 18 chords, L 1.04 m, pinned ends: True, columns at ends: 12
!      ring r 8.5: 18 chords, L 2.95 m, pinned ends: True, columns at ends: 0
!      ring r 12.0: 18 chords, L 4.17 m, pinned ends: False, columns at ends: 18
!   group 11, RHS 150x150x10: 18 lines, V-column raker, ground to L1, L 5.81-5.82 m, 44-44 deg to the horizontal, z 0.0->4.05, switch #COL
!   group 12, RHS 150x150x10: 9 lines, raker, ground to L1, L 5.35-5.36 m, 49-49 deg to the horizontal, z 0.0->4.05, switch #COL
!   group 13, RHS 150x150x10: 20 lines, vertical column, L 4.00-4.05 m, 90-90 deg to the horizontal, z 0.0->4.05, 4.05->8.05, switch #COL
!   group 14, RHS 150x150x10: 6 lines, vertical column, ground to L1, L 4.05-4.05 m, 90-90 deg to the horizontal, z 0.0->4.05, switch #COL
!   group 21, RHS 150x150x10: 18 lines, V-column raker, L1 to L2, L 5.78-5.78 m, 44-44 deg to the horizontal, z 4.05->8.05, switch #COL
!   group 23, RHS 150x150x10: 2 lines, vertical column, L1 to L2, L 4.00-4.00 m, 90-90 deg to the horizontal, z 4.05->8.05, switch #COL
!   group 24, RHS 150x150x10: 6 lines, vertical column, L1 to L2, L 4.00-4.00 m, 90-90 deg to the horizontal, z 4.05->8.05, switch #COL
!   group 31, RHS 150x150x10: 18 lines, V-column raker, L2 to roof, L 5.78-5.78 m, 44-44 deg to the horizontal, z 8.05->12.06, switch #COL
!   group 34, RHS 150x150x10: 6 lines, vertical column, L2 to roof, L 4.00-4.00 m, 90-90 deg to the horizontal, z 8.05->12.06, switch #COL   <-- REMOVED in v15
!   group 60, RHS 50x50x5: 20 lines, stair landing member, L 0.49-1.30 m, 0-0 deg to the horizontal, z 6.04->6.04, switch #LAND
!   group 60, RHS 250x150x16: 22 lines, stair stringer, post or landing beam, L 0.43-3.98 m, 0-37 deg to the horizontal, z 4.05->6.04, 6.04->6.04, 6.28->8.05, switch #STR
!   group 60, tread 300x5: 42 tread lines, NOT checked (5 mm plates spanning 2.1 m between the stringers: no member buckling)
!   8 stubs shorter than 0.3 m, NOT checked (no buckling length, section check by AQB):
!      SLN 76 (0.12 m, group 60), SLN 77 (0.24 m, group 60), SLN 93 (0.24 m, group 60), SLN 98 (0.12 m, group 60)
!      SLN 473 (0.12 m, group 60), SLN 474 (0.24 m, group 60), SLN 475 (0.24 m, group 60), SLN 476 (0.12 m, group 60)
!   SLN 74, SLN 75: line supports (SLNS FIX PP, no section), not members, nothing to check
!   shells (SAR, kingpost plates and the ground slab) are not members: no BDK check
!
+PROG BDK urs:9001
HEAD 26016 buckling of all members - EN 1993-1-1 6.3 (UK NA values), ULS 101-154 (no 136-139 from v13), envelope LC 9100
ECHO FULL NO
ECHO SUM FULL        $ one line per member with its governing combination, EXTR = every member and every combination
ECHO PLOT NO

$ ---------- settings: which members ----------
STO#L15   1          $ 1 = check L1 deck beams, group 15 (UB 254x146x43)
STO#L25   1          $ 1 = check L2 deck beams, group 25 (UB 457x191x89)
STO#L35   1          $ 1 = check roof beams, group 35 (UB 254x146x43)
STO#RING  1          $ 1 = check the ring beams at r 12 and r 8.5 as well
STO#RING3 0          $ 1 = also the short rings at r 3.0 (and r 1.9 on L1)
STO#COL   1          $ 1 = check the SHS 150x150x10 columns and rakers (groups 11, 12, 13, 14, 21, 23, 24, 31, 34; group 34 removed in v15)
STO#STR   1          $ 1 = check the RHS 200x100x6 stair stringers, posts and landing beams (group 60), the SHS 100x100x5 landing posts (group 61) and the external stair (group 62, v17)
STO#LAND  1          $ 1 = check the RHS 50x50x5 stair landing members (group 60)
STO#PAT   1          $ 1 = also the pattern combinations 151-154 (in the unified file since 16 Oct 2026), 0 = 101-148 only
$ ---------- settings: restraints (UB beams) and frame ----------
STO#JOIN  1          $ 1 = L1/roof radial beams as one continuous member (MEMB + CONT), 0 = each structural line on its own
STO#AUTO  0          $ 1 = end supports from a linear analysis of the whole model (AUTO), 0 = fork supports (all members)
STO#DXR   0          $ kNm/rad twist spring where only pinned ring beams meet the radial beam (0 = none, 1E9 = practically fixed)
STO#EZR   0          $ mm height of the ring-beam lateral restraint above (-) or below (+) the beam axis, 0 = shear centre
STO#DECK  0          $ 1 = deck panels restrain the top flange of the L1 + L2 deck beams laterally (CVL HDIV #NPART, EZ TOP)
STO#DECKR 0          $ 1 = the same for the roof beams (group 35)
STO#NPART 8          $ number of equal parts per member for the top-flange restraint points when DECK = 1
STO#SWAY  0          $ 1 = sway frame (alpha_cr < 10, forces from a TH2 run): Cmy = Cmz = 0.9 for the columns, Table B.3
STO#COLD  0          $ 1 = the hollow sections are cold formed (EN 10219): LTB curve c instead of b (and AQUA BCY/BCZ 'C', see header)

$ ---------- code settings ----------
TVAR NAME GAM-S1 VAL 1.0 SCOP DESI                       $ gamma_M1 = 1.00, UK NA NA.2.15 (= EN)
$   every member group below restates its full CTRL line and the LC list (CTRL persists item by item): SCL AUTO = class
$   from AQB and 6.3.2.3, CURV = LTB curve, MTHD 2 = Annex B, LTB AUTO = Table B.1 / B.2 by section type, TAB NO = kc
$   from C1, SWY / SWZ = sway frame (Cm 0.9), LCST 9100 = store the utilisation envelope as LC 9100

$ ---------- combinations: calculated load cases of 26016_loads_unified.dat (MAXIMA envelopes cannot be used), listed after
$   every CTRL line below with generation instructions, a comma list being limited to about 25 values ----------

$ ====================================================================================================
$ L1 - group 15 - UB 254x146x43 - LTB curve B (UK NA Table NA.1, h/b 1.76), Table B.2 factors
$ ====================================================================================================
IF #L15>0
CTRL OPT EN SCL AUTO CURV B MTHD 2 BETA 0.75 LLT0 0.4 TAB NO LTB AUTO SWY NO SWZ NO LCST 9100
$ v10 reduced list (see 26016_v9_load_review): 145-148 contain 102 (+EHF), 119-126 contain 103-106/111-118/127-130
$   for every gravity-governed effect, 107-110 govern every uplift/reversal effect; 135 affects the stairs only
LC (107 110 1)       $ 1.0G + 1.5W uplift: reversal (bottom-flange compression)
LC (119 126 1)       $ Q lead + 0.75W down, W lead + 1.05Q down
LC (145 148 1)       $ 1.35G + 1.5Q + EHF (contains 102)
IF #PAT>0
  LC (151 154 1)     $ the live-load pattern combinations (deck beams only)
ENDIF
