$ v14: the stair members get their own BDK program. In v12 and v13 BDK stopped with error 31 "design sections for load case
$   135 could not be generated" as soon as a 21st distinct load case appeared after the 20 of the beam/column lists
$   (107-110, 119-126, 145-148, 151-154); LC 135 itself is an ordinary computed case with ordinary loads. Keeping each BDK
$   program at <= 20 load cases avoids that. Envelope of this program: LC 9101 (the first program keeps 9100).
+PROG BDK urs:9003
HEAD 26016 buckling of the stair members - EN 1993-1-1 6.3 (UK NA values), envelope LC 9101
ECHO FULL NO
ECHO SUM FULL
ECHO PLOT NO
STO#STR   1          $ 1 = check the RHS 200x100x6 stair stringers, posts and landing beams (group 60), the SHS 100x100x5 landing posts (group 61) and the external stair (group 62, v17)
STO#LAND  1          $ 1 = check the RHS 50x50x5 stair landing members (group 60)
STO#AUTO  0          $ as in the first program
STO#SWAY  0
STO#COLD  0
TVAR NAME GAM-S1 VAL 1.0 SCOP DESI                       $ gamma_M1 = 1.00

$ ====================================================================================================
$ stair stringers, posts and landing beams - RHS 250x150x16 (section 5), 22 lines, group 60 - flexural buckling + interaction (chi_LT = 1), each line alone, fork ends
$ ====================================================================================================
IF #STR>0
IF #COLD>0
  CTRL OPT EN SCL AUTO CURV C MTHD 2 BETA 0.75 LLT0 0.4 TAB NO LTB AUTO SWY NO SWZ NO LCST 9101
ELSE
  CTRL OPT EN SCL AUTO CURV B MTHD 2 BETA 0.75 LLT0 0.4 TAB NO LTB AUTO SWY NO SWZ NO LCST 9101
ENDIF
$ v10 reduced list (see 26016_v9_load_review): as the deck beams, plus 135 (stair barriers inward), no deck patterns; v13 no temperature
LC (107 110 1)       $ 1.0G + 1.5W uplift: stair flights get wind uplift (VF)
LC (119 126 1)       $ Q lead + 0.75W down, W lead + 1.05Q down
LC (135 135 1)       $ barriers inward
LC (145 148 1)       $ 1.35G + 1.5Q + EHF (contains 102)
$ group 60 SLN 79: stair stringer, post or landing beam, RHS 250x150x16, L 2.96 m, z 6.28 -> 8.05, 37 deg to the horizontal, fork ends, Lcr = L
IF #AUTO>0
  CVA CB 0 CY AUTO CZ AUTO DX AUTO DY AUTO DZ AUTO
  CVE CB 0 CY AUTO CZ AUTO DX AUTO DY AUTO DZ AUTO
ELSE
  CVA CB 0 CY FIX CZ FIX DX FIX DY 0 DZ 0            $ fork support
  CVE CB 0 CY FIX CZ FIX DX FIX DY 0 DZ 0
ENDIF
