$ ===================== ALPHA_CR SWAY CHECK (LTB thread, unchanged) =====================
!#!Info 26016 HPC Kier BAM JV - frame sway check: buckling factor alpha_cr (EN 1993-1-1 5.2.1) for the governing ULS cases
!
! Version 2, 2026-10-16 (v1 reviewed independently against the ASE manual). UNTESTED in SOFiSTiK. Run in the 26016
! project AFTER 26016_loads_unified.dat (it needs the solved load cases 102, 119, 145-148). Needs the ASE eigenvalue
! licence (the one the eigenfrequency run used); the TH2 block at the end needs the non-linear licence as well.
!
! WHY: 26016_buckling_all_bdk.dat checks every column and raker between its end nodes with pinned ends, Lcr = L. That is
!   the non-sway assumption, allowed when alpha_cr >= 10 (5.2.1(3)): the factor on the design loads at which the whole
!   frame buckles elastically. Each ASE program below takes the internal forces of one ULS combination as the primary
!   stress state (SYST PLC) and computes the lowest 20 buckling load factors of the whole model (EIGE ... BUCK, LMIN AUTO
!   = first positive eigenvalue), stored as mode shapes in 20 load cases from 9201, 9221, 9241, 9261, 9281 and 9301
!   (free numbers: BDK envelope 9100, MAXIMA 4101+, eigenfrequencies 2001-2110). Syntax as in the shipped example
!   lateral_buckling.dat (SYST PLC n / EIGE n BUCK LC m LMIN AUTO); a linear primary load case is the documented case.
!
! HOW TO READ THE RESULT: the output lists the buckling load factors per primary load case. alpha_cr is the smallest
!   positive factor that belongs to a GLOBAL (sway) mode. 20 modes are asked for because the lowest ones may all be
!   local: a compressed stair stringer, an RHS 50x50x5 landing member, a kingpost shell panel. Look at the mode shapes
!   in the Animator / WinGRAF (LC 9201 ...): a mode that bends one stair member or one shell panel is local and does not
!   count for the frame (it does tell you that member is close to buckling, note it), a mode that sways a whole level
!   does count. If all 20 are local, raise the number in EIGE or suppress the stair and shell modes with FIXT (ASE
!   manual, record FIXT: FIXT NODE ALL FIX, then FIXT NODE ALL FREE inside boxes around the frame).
!   - alpha_cr >= 10 in every case here: the frame is non-sway, the BDK file is complete as it stands.
!   - 3 <= alpha_cr < 10: switch on the -PROG ASE block at the end (second-order re-run of every combination that carries
!     the sway imperfection EHF: 103-130 and 141-148), then run the BDK file again with #SWAY 1 (Cmy = Cmz = 0.9 for the
!     columns, Table B.3). The member lengths stay Lcr = L, 5.2.2(7)b, because second-order effects and the imperfection
!     are then in the member forces. 101-102, 135-139 and 151-154 carry no EHF: for the columns 145-148 cover 102, and
!     the audit thread can add EHF to 135-139 / 151-154 if you want them covered too. The TH2 run OVERWRITES the linear
!     results of those load cases, so re-run the MAXIMA part of the unified file afterwards if its envelopes are used.
!   - alpha_cr < 3: the structure is very sway-sensitive, a full second-order analysis (TH3) with imperfections of
!     every combination is needed before any member check.
!
! CASES: 102 = 1.35G + 1.5Q (largest column compression), 119 = G + Q + psi W +X with the roof pushed down,
!   145-148 = 1.35G + 1.5Q + EHF in each direction (the sway-imperfection cases). Add any other PLC by copying a block.
!
+PROG ASE urs:9201
HEAD 26016 buckling factors, PLC 102 (1.35G + 1.5Q)
SYST PLC 102
EIGE 20 BUCK LC 9201 LMIN AUTO
END

+PROG ASE urs:9202
HEAD 26016 buckling factors, PLC 119 (G + Q + psi W +X, roof down)
SYST PLC 119
EIGE 20 BUCK LC 9221 LMIN AUTO
END

-PROG ASE urs:9203     $ v10: OFF - EHF is 0.3 % of the vertical load, alpha_cr of 145 = alpha_cr of 102 (urs:9201)
HEAD 26016 buckling factors, PLC 145 (1.35G + 1.5Q + EHF +X)
SYST PLC 145
EIGE 20 BUCK LC 9241 LMIN AUTO
END

-PROG ASE urs:9204     $ v10: OFF - EHF is 0.3 % of the vertical load, alpha_cr of 146 = alpha_cr of 102 (urs:9201)
HEAD 26016 buckling factors, PLC 146 (1.35G + 1.5Q + EHF -X)
SYST PLC 146
EIGE 20 BUCK LC 9261 LMIN AUTO
END

-PROG ASE urs:9205     $ v10: OFF - EHF is 0.3 % of the vertical load, alpha_cr of 147 = alpha_cr of 102 (urs:9201)
HEAD 26016 buckling factors, PLC 147 (1.35G + 1.5Q + EHF -Y)
SYST PLC 147
EIGE 20 BUCK LC 9281 LMIN AUTO
END

-PROG ASE urs:9206     $ v10: OFF - EHF is 0.3 % of the vertical load, alpha_cr of 148 = alpha_cr of 102 (urs:9201)
HEAD 26016 buckling factors, PLC 148 (1.35G + 1.5Q + EHF +Y)
SYST PLC 148
EIGE 20 BUCK LC 9301 LMIN AUTO
END

-PROG ASE urs:9210     $ switch on with +PROG only if alpha_cr < 10: second-order (P-delta) re-run of the EHF combinations
HEAD 26016 second-order (TH2) re-run of the combinations that carry the sway imperfection EHF
SYST PROB TH2
LC (103 130 1)         $ the same COPY-built load cases, now solved with P-delta effects, results overwrite the linear ones
LC (141 148 1)
END

$ ===================== AQB CROSS-SECTION CHECK (member-check thread, added) =====================
!#!Chapter AQB steel cross-section check EN 1993-1-1 6.2, all steel beams, ULS 101-154 (no 136-139 from v13)
+PROG AQB urs:9501
HEAD 26016 steel cross-section resistance EN 1993-1-1 6.2, all beams, ULS 101-154 (no 136-139 from v13)
ECHO FORC NO
ECHO SECT NO
ECHO COMB NO
ECHO STRE NO
ECHO C2T  YES
ECHO USEP YES
CTRL MSEL STEE
BEAM TYPE BEAM
LC (101 130 1) TYPE (D)
LC (135 135 1) TYPE (D)
LC (141 148 1) TYPE (D)
LC (151 154 1) TYPE (D)
STRE C M0
END
